# Requests for the REST Client (VS Code) / HTTP Client (Rider, Visual Studio).
# Run `POST rooms` first and paste the returned id into @roomId, then do the same for @bookingId.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5249/api/v1
@roomId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@bookingId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@userId = 3f2504e0-4f89-41d3-9a0c-0305e82c3301

### Create a room
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Meeting Room A",
  "capacity": 8,
  "hourlyRate": 25.00,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### List active rooms
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms?isActive=true

### Available rooms for a slot ('+' must be URL-encoded as %2B)
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/available?start=2030-01-15T10:00:00%2B02:00&end=2030-01-15T12:00:00%2B02:00&minCapacity=4

### Book the room
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": "{{roomId}}",
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "start": "2030-01-15T10:00:00+02:00",
  "end": "2030-01-15T12:00:00+02:00",
  "attendees": 4
}

### Get the booking
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}

### Confirm
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}/confirm

### Cancel (returns the refund)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel

### A user's bookings
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/bookings?status=Confirmed&page=1&pageSize=20

### Health
GET http://localhost:5249/health/ready
